The open-staging loop (lines 610-618) reads only this --out's staging.log. _check_leftovers returns early when neither file exists (lines 583-584), and collect with --void removes both files without checking them (lines 704-705, 740-743). t_crossdir.py does the following:
- stage xa audit-01 into ws-xd;
- remove packet.txt (as an agent that rewrites it, or a slip, would);
- stage xc case-0001 into the same folder: rc 0, although xa's staging is still open;
- write the case answer;
- collect xa audit-01 --void: 'VOID: packet.txt removed'. audit-01.attempt-1.json raw starts '{"case_id": "a1_r1-F06-2"...', and the folder is now empty;
- collect xc case-0001 is refused: 'the workspace no longer holds case-0001; ... record the attempt with --void'.
A second route works the same way with packets that are byte-identical in two --out folders (audit-packets is deterministic for a salt). With an open staging of out-audit-2 audit-01 in ws-a1, stage out-audit audit-08 into ws-a1 returned rc 0 and overwrote packet.txt, because out-audit has a collected staging with the same bytes. AG1 makes one workspace shared by all jobs, and the brief says stage refuses a workspace whose staging has no collected attempt.

_model_label is called for voids too (line 708, lines 655-657). t_label.py does the following:
- collect audit-01 with 'Gemini 3 Pro' writes model.json;
- collect audit-02 --model 'Claude Sonnet' --void '...' is refused: 'the model label in this folder is 'Gemini 3 Pro'; a different label needs --model-change';
- the same command with --model-change succeeds, and model.json now lists 'Claude Sonnet' as the current label;
- collect audit-03 --model 'Gemini 3 Pro' is then refused: 'the model label in this folder is 'Claude Sonnet''.
